  ! #244: "Assistant sources list: Citations in assistant answers are now listed as a numbered Sources list below the answer. An answer without citations shows no empty Sources block." - The Sources list below the answer was the interim #244 integration state, and #245 re-adds inline badges while keeping the sources list for unanchored citations. The 'no empty Sources block' claim comes from #233. Presenting it as a separate new feature is misleading.
  ! #218: "You can count on that check having run for every answer drawn from the knowledge base" - #218 says the check is forced only once, on the first turn after passages appear. It guarantees at least one check after any retrieval, not that every passage or answer was grounded. The claim overstates this.
  ! #245: "a citation the answer does not quote by title still appears in that list, as long as the assistant quotes the passage title word for word, which it is instructed to do." - The facts say a citation whose title does not appear stays in the sources list only. Anchoring (not the list entry) depends on the model quoting the title verbatim. The sentence garbles this condition.
  ! #213: "Board card titles no longer get cut off mid-letter." - The design-token PR (#213) says the card titles clipped mid-glyph and that it fixed this with flex: 0 0 auto. Listing it under 'Consistent look across pages' attributes it to the wrong feature, though the fix itself is supported.

